  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Reducing Community-Level Vulnerabilities to Trafficking in Persons in Moldova</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The project targets a two-fold problem: first, poor prevention, identification, and referral capacities in vulnerable communities, and second, low rates of VoT engagement with prosecution efforts. The project will do so by improving local actors&#x2019; prevention capacities in vulnerable communities, improve attitudes to participation in judicial proceedings among VoTs, which will lead to increased participation in community-level and central-level TiP response services in Moldova. The project will support community-level identification and referral pathways, implement a communications campaign targeting the Roma community, and work towards strengthening victim-centered collaboration between investigation, prosecution and social assistance actors.</narrative>
  </description>
